{
  "version": "0.1",
  "note": "Cue palettes (0.24 M5). The audio planner picks a palette from the art-direction look (ProjectMeta.art.look), else from the temperament, and draws every cue family from it. Families are listed in preference order; a later family is used only when an earlier one would exceed 40% of the video's cues. role_lufs are the loudness each role is normalised to (gain_db = role_lufs - sound.lufs, plus a deterministic jitter of at most 0.9 dB). Roles: open = first arrival, hero = the beat's lead reveal, hero_big_with = beds played with the video's biggest hero, riser = lead-in before that hero, transition = the cut whoosh, small = secondary arrivals, close = tail bed when the last beat is not the biggest. (0.24 M7) count = the family of a counting number's tick train (one tick per 1/N of its eased progress, never on the settle); count_lock = the soft hit on the settle when the beat's hero is elsewhere; count_max_per_s caps the train's rate; count_offset_db shifts the train's loudness. voice = the levels under a voice-over (LUFS-equiv, so every cue sits at least 12 LU below the voice while a word is spoken): per role while speaking, plus gap_boost_db in gaps between phrases (a gap is 0.25 s without a word), nucleus_db on a word's middle half, count_speech_db extra for ticks while speaking, count_max_per_s_speech the train rate cap under speech.",
